{"Title":"An Act to provide for the future information technology needs of Massachusetts","BillNumber":"H4889","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":null,"Name":"Future Information Technology Needs","Type":2,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2024-07-19T15:17:50.237"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"GOV7","Name":"Maura T. Healey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/GOV7","ResponseDate":"2024-01-09T10:52:53.7"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4889/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"The committee of conference on the disagreeing votes of the two branches with reference to the Senate amendment of the House Bill to provide for the future information technology needs of Massachusetts (House, No. 4648), reports recommending passage of the accompanying bill (House, No. 4889).  ","DocumentText":null,"EmergencyPreamble":"Whereas, The deferred operation of this act would tend to defeat its purpose, which is to provide forthwith for the information technology and security needs of the commonwealth and deploy broadband access to the citizens of the commonwealth, therefore it is hereby declared to be an emergency law, necessary for the immediate preservation of the public convenience.\r\n\r\n","RollCalls":[{"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Branch":"Senate","RollCallNumber":220,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Branches/Senate/RollCalls/220"}],"Attachments":[{"Description":"IT Bond - 11A Report","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=18913&title=IT%20Bond%20-%2011A%20Report"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Compromised Version","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":null},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}